d estimating equation models with autoregressive correlation structure\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"IRRs and ratios of observed-to-expected case numbers were adjusted for district-wide weekly COVID-19 non–school-associated (community) attack rates\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"estimated using a comparative interrupted time series model among students and staff members in a subset of 26 districts\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"Statistical significance was defined as p<0.05.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Models used an autoregressive correlation structure of order 1 with a log population offset.\"}], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"uncertain_fields\": []}", "type": "text"}]}